// HARD RULE: never set SWIFT_STRICT_CONCURRENCY (or any setting below) on the
// `xcodebuild` command line or project-wide. A command-line setting also
// applies to the SwiftPM package targets, and in CatCareCalendar
// SWIFT_STRICT_CONCURRENCY = complete crashed the Swift compiler on the
// FirebaseAuth package target. Set these on TTB's own targets only, one
// target at a time, never at the project level.


// StrictConcurrency.xcconfig
//
// Measured settings for the staged Swift 6 concurrency migration.
// Full measurements, diagnostic categories and rationale:
//   docs/swift6-concurrency-assessment.md
//
// Every setting in this file is commented out, and no target is based on this
// file. It changes NOTHING. It is committed unwired on purpose, so that the
// first commit of this migration does not touch project.pbxproj and cannot
// conflict with an in-flight branch.
//
// Wiring note: the TTB app target's Debug and Release configurations are
// already based on TTB/Secrets.xcconfig, and a configuration takes only one
// base file. Git ignores TTB/Secrets.xcconfig, so an #include added there is
// never committed. To wire this file into the app target, set the stage's
// setting on the target directly, or add the #include to
// TTB/Secrets.xcconfig.template and to every local TTB/Secrets.xcconfig. The
// two test targets have no base file today.
//
// Measured 2026-10-03 on Apple Swift 6.4 (swiftlang-6.4.0.34.1) / Xcode 27.0
// (27A266a), base main @ ca435bb, Debug configuration,
// 'generic/platform=iOS Simulator', IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET = 18.2,
// SWIFT_VERSION = 5.0. Counts are unique repository diagnostics. Baseline: the
// app target has 0 errors and 12 warnings in 5 files (181/181 files compiled);
// the unit test target has 1 warning. Re-measure on a new toolchain before you
// trust these counts.


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Stage 1 - UI test target (TTBUITests)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Measured 2026-10-03: ** TEST BUILD SUCCEEDED **, 718 warnings -> 56.
// With `complete` alone the UI tests report 718 warnings in 14 of 14 files,
// all main-actor access from a nonisolated XCTest method (XCUIApplication is
// main-actor-isolated). Adding main-actor-by-default removes 662 of them.
//
// Apply to TTBUITests ONLY. Do not apply main-actor-by-default to TTBTests
// without measuring it first.
//
//   SWIFT_STRICT_CONCURRENCY = complete
//   SWIFT_DEFAULT_ACTOR_ISOLATION = MainActor
//
// 56 override-isolation warnings remain: 14 files x 4 - init(),
// init(invocation:), init(selector:), setUpWithError(). Each is now
// main-actor-isolated while the XCTestCase declaration it overrides is
// nonisolated. Run the UI tests on iPhone 12 / iOS 26.5 after this stage.
//
// APPLIED 2026-10-04 (issue #45): both settings are set directly on the
// TTBUITests target, Debug and Release; this file stays unwired. Re-measured
// on the same toolchain, base main @ cfcc9b9: baseline 0, `complete` alone 717
// (one fewer than 2026-10-03), both settings 56, after the fix 0.
//
// The fix: each test class is `nonisolated final class X: XCTestCase`, holding
// only its constants and setUpWithError(), and every test and helper sits in an
// `@MainActor extension X`. The CCC fix (an explicit @MainActor class, and
// setUp() async throws) clears setUpWithError() only: the inherited
// initializers stay main-actor, and init(invocation:) cannot be overridden
// because NSInvocation is unavailable in Swift.


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Stage 2 - app target (TTB), warning mode
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Measured 2026-10-03: 202 warnings in 40 files, 0 errors, 181/181 files
// compiled, build succeeds. A second build produced the identical list. No
// blocker to clear first.
//
// APPLIED (issue #46): set directly on the TTB target's Debug and Release
// configurations in project.pbxproj, not through this file; the line below
// stays commented out and this file stays unwired. Re-measured
// 2026-10-04 on base main @ cfcc9b9: 0 errors, 202 warnings in 40 files,
// 181/181 files compiled - unchanged from 2026-10-03.
//
//   SWIFT_STRICT_CONCURRENCY = complete
//
// SWIFT_STRICT_CONCURRENCY = targeted is not offered: measured 2026-10-03 at
// 29 warnings in 11 files. It gives no safety that `complete` does not, and it
// hides the 112 region-isolation warnings that are the bulk of the work.


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Stage 3 - unit test target (TTBTests), warning mode
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Measured 2026-10-03: 31 warnings in 8 files (baseline 1), 0 errors, 49/49
// files compiled. Do not skip this stage: CatCareCalendar skipped its test
// targets here and its first SWIFT_VERSION = 6.0 attempt failed on the UI
// tests.
//
//   SWIFT_STRICT_CONCURRENCY = complete
//
// APPLIED 2026-10-04 (issue #47): set directly on the TTBTests Debug and
// Release configurations in project.pbxproj. Re-measured on base main @
// cfcc9b9 with the Appendix A method: 1 warning -> 31 warnings in 8 files,
// 0 errors, 49/49 files compiled; the app target stayed at 12.


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Stage 4 - source fixes by category
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Tickets 4.1-4.10 in the assessment. It has no setting.


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Stage 5 - app target, default actor isolation (DECIDE ON EVIDENCE, NOT NOW)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Two separate settings, two separate decisions, after stage 4.
//
// Measured 2026-10-03, on top of `complete`: 202 warnings in 32 files, 0
// errors, 181/181 files compiled. Net change 0 (202 -> 202): it removes all
// of categories B (73) and F (9) and most of G, and adds 93 new warnings that
// move the cost into the service actors.
// Re-measure after stage 4 and choose then.
//
//   SWIFT_DEFAULT_ACTOR_ISOLATION = MainActor
//
// Measured 2026-10-03, on top of `complete` alone: the BUILD FAILS, 26 errors
// (all in Services/InMemoryQuestionListShareService.swift) and 42 warnings,
// 112/181 files compiled. On top of main-actor-by-default it changes nothing:
// 202 warnings in 32 files, identical list. Find the cause of the 26 errors
// before you turn it on.
//
//   SWIFT_UPCOMING_FEATURE_NONISOLATED_NONSENDING_BY_DEFAULT = YES


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Stage 6 - language mode, LAST
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Flip this only when stages 2 and 3 report 0 warnings AND 0 macro-expansion
// diagnostics. Set it on all 6 configurations, then remove
// SWIFT_STRICT_CONCURRENCY (Swift 6 implies `complete`).
//
// Measured 2026-10-03 on the app target: the BUILD FAILS, 22 errors and 4
// warnings, 158/181 files compiled. That is a lower bound, because error mode
// stops the module before every file reports. On the test targets: 13 errors
// and 12 unit-test warnings in 7 files, 18/49 unit files and 0/14 UI files
// compiled.
//
// It does NOT raise the minimum iOS version: no build in any stage produced an
// availability diagnostic against iOS 18.2.
//
//   SWIFT_VERSION = 6.0
//
// Keep Task.immediate, InlineArray and withTaskPriorityEscalationHandler out of
// the app target: each carries an iOS 26.0 floor (CatCareCalendar probe).
// Synchronization.Mutex (iOS 18.0) fits. isolated deinit was probed on 18.4
// only and is unverified on 18.2.


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Measurement aid, not a shipping setting
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Measured 2026-10-03 on top of SWIFT_VERSION = 6.0: 37 errors and 9 warnings,
// but coverage FELL from 158/181 to 135/181 files, and the two runs disagree on
// which files they saw. It does not help error mode. That is the reason this
// migration measures in warning mode and flips the language mode once, at the
// end.
//
//   OTHER_SWIFT_FLAGS = $(inherited) -continue-building-after-errors
